```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Agentic LLM serving with bursty per-session KV pressure where sessions incur tool-call or downstream idle gaps (median ~1-2 s, tail to 30 s) and resume with high prefix re-reference probability (p_rr >= 0.7). Example: agents invoking APIs, retrieval, or multi-step workflows that pause between turns.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-leaning; simulation shows large Pareto wins (e.g., 4096-token prefix: 68.3 ms evict-recompute vs ~0.02 ms prefetch, 3413x; 8192-token: 136.5 ms vs 0.28 ms, 488x) inside a narrow "sane-deployment box" (BW >=16 GB/s, C <=8, prefix <=256 blocks/224 MiB, gap >=1 s, p_rr >=0.7) with 1 loss in 7560 cells. Outside that box the policy loses 13-50x (e.g., 512-block prefix, 8 GB/s, C=32, p_rr=0.5, gap=0.2 s: fetch 3.48 s vs recompute 0.07-0.27 s). The win collapses under PCIe contention (70% of 6.5% loss cells are BW-bound; loss fingerprint: gap <=0.5 s 75%, C >=16 90%, prefix >=256 blocks 73%, BW 8 GB/s 63%). Evidence is L0 analytic+Monte-Carlo, CPU-only, stdlib-only, SERIAL, with NO GPU/model/network; gap model is LogNormal placeholder, PCIe BW is fair-share nameplate not measured under concurrent D2H/H2D+decode traffic, and re-reference is a swept parameter not a measured agent statistic (ORCHESTRATOR CAVEAT). Real vLLM/LMCache offload resume-TTFT vs recompute not measured.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Integration into vLLM/SGLang to track per-session gaps and schedule proactive demote+prefetch; host-memory capacity/management; misprediction waste when p_rr < 1 inflates effective concurrency C/p_rr; PCIe BW shared with decode/prefill traffic (not modeled) lowering effective B_total; need for accurate gap distribution—real sub-second mass decides kill-corner but LogNormal is unvalidated; operational complexity vs simpler reactive CPU-swap (vLLM) or evict-recompute which degrades gracefully under load while prefetch collapses on contended link]
RATIONALE: Packet EXP-0019 reports PARTIAL win-region (93.5% Pareto wins, 89.7% gap-hides-fetch) but explicitly scopes claim: "strictly better Pareto is NOT universal — it has a clean PCIe-bandwidth-under-concurrency boundary" (L0 RESULTS). Sane-box (BW>=16 GB/s, C<=8, prefix<=256 blocks) yields 1/7560 losses; kill-corner (short gap, high C, large prefix, low BW, low p_rr, fast prefill) flips win to 13-50x loss (THE CRUX). Prior-art caveat concedes KV offload is NOT novel (vLLM CPU-swap reactive, LMCache cross-instance, FlexGen, InfiniGen, layer-wise); claimed narrow novelty is gap-timed proactive, untested against real vLLM swap path. L1 must measure real PCIe/NVLink-C2C BW under concurrency, real offload resume-TTFT, real agent gap distribution, real re-reference prob—none present in L0 (What a real GPU L1 should measure). Therefore operational significance is plausible but unproven; negative result is actionable guidance to scope deployment or fall back to evict-recompute.
```
